        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:workHistory.responsibilities.0",
        "expected": "The responsibilities I've held have mostly been end-to-end ownership rather than isolated tickets. At Summer Atlantic Capital / SAC Nexus, I own major parts of the machine-learning core of an anomaly-detection system: the repository and CI scaffold, the event-ingestion pipeline, a versioned FastAPI microservice, the public detection API, temporal sequence modeling over event streams, and a learning-to-rank layer that prioritizes alerts. I added a retrieval-augmented explanation layer because an anomaly system that floods analysts with alerts creates a second problem instead of solving the first. At Intelehealth, I built a resource-availability scoring pipeline in Python across 32 villages and designed an evaluation framework comparing AI-generated clinical outputs against a 4,169-case clinical standard using stratified sampling. As technical lead for ClarityAtlas, I built the iOS product end to end in Swift, SwiftUI, and Supabase, including a passive sleep-estimation system using HealthKit and Core Motion signals, and shipped it into a live Hopkins pilot with 30+ users. In each case I was responsible not only for writing the system but for documenting failure modes and making sure it held up with real users.",
        "observed": "Built and shipped a compliance-scoring layer across 4 financial-risk workflows (KYC, transactions, escrow, AML), cutting KYC case-reconstruction time by 1–3 minutes per review and transaction review by 1–2 minutes per payment — roughly 4 analyst-hours/day across 80 daily scored cases. Developed an AML candidate-ranking and explanation system that compressed a 45-minute partner-screening workflow to 15–20 minutes (a 56–67% reduction), saving 4–5 analyst-hours per week per analyst; modeled at $20K/year of labor capacity per analyst, or $200K/year across a 10-analyst deployment. Implemented fail-closed escrow routing that eliminated a false-safe failure mode where missing risk inputs scored 0 and could yield a misleading Low-risk result. Built the service from an empty repository: 7 REST endpoints on a versioned FastAPI microservice, a unified event layer across 3 categories for cross-agent escalation, 114 tests, and CI at 80% branch coverage.",
